    "updated_at": "2023-07-26T11:49:43Z",
    "body": "> You can do this today without issue\r\n\r\nThe issue seems to be that all custom attributes must be prefixed with `data-`, so an attribute prefixed with `js-` is non-conforming.\r\n\r\n> Cannot add any more buttons since they will implement not only visual, but logical behavior\r\n\r\nI think that this is something to do with jQuery, but in normal JS, an event listener applied to an element that has been selected from a class selector, will only work on that element, and no other elements with that same class. And it will still work once that class has been removed",
